---
title: Our Values and Vision
summary: GCUA's mission, vision, and core values shape our faith, education, and ministry.
---

# Our Mission

To prepare and empower Spirit-filled Christian leaders to proclaim the Gospel, fulfill the Great Commission, and serve Christ effectively throughout the world.

# Our Vision

To develop Christ-centered, biblically grounded, and Holy Spirit-empowered leaders who make disciples and advance God's Kingdom.

We envision graduates who demonstrate spiritual maturity, strong biblical knowledge, and effective ministry skills. They will serve as transformational leaders in churches, families, communities, and nations.

Our vision is to raise Christian leaders who impact the world through the Gospel of Jesus Christ.

# Our Core Values

Our core values reflect our commitment to biblical truth, spiritual growth, Christian leadership, and Spirit-empowered ministry.

## 1. The Authority of Scripture

We believe the Bible is the inspired, infallible, and inerrant Word of God. It is the foundation of our faith, education, and ministry.

**Biblical reference:** 2 Timothy 3:16–17.

## 2. Reconciliation Through Christ

We believe God reconciles humanity to Himself through Jesus Christ. We are called to share His message of salvation and reconciliation with the world.

**Biblical references:** 2 Corinthians 5:18–20; Colossians 1:19–20.

## 3. The Lordship of Jesus Christ

We affirm Jesus Christ as the Head of the Church and Lord of every believer. His life and teachings guide our faith, character, and service.

**Biblical references:** Ephesians 5:23; Romans 1:4; 1 Corinthians 1:23–24.

## 4. Empowerment of the Holy Spirit

We believe the Holy Spirit continues to work supernaturally today. He guides, transforms, and empowers believers through His presence and spiritual gifts.

**Biblical references:** Acts 1:8; John 14:12–17; John 16:13; 1 Corinthians 4:20; 2 Corinthians 3:5–18; 1 Thessalonians 1:5.

## 5. Every Believer Called to Ministry

We believe every Christian is uniquely gifted and called to serve God. We encourage believers to discover their calling and develop their gifts for effective ministry.

**Biblical references:** Ephesians 4:11–16; 2 Corinthians 3:5–6; 2 Corinthians 5:18.

## 6. Fellowship and Partnership With God

We believe effective ministry begins with a close relationship with God. Through prayer, obedience, and dependence on the Holy Spirit, believers participate in His work.

**Biblical references:** Psalm 103:7; Hebrews 3:10; Isaiah 55:8; John 15:14–16; 2 Corinthians 5:20; 2 Corinthians 6:1; Philippians 2:12–13.

## 7. Living for God's Glory

We believe our highest purpose is to glorify God and enjoy His presence forever. Our lives should honor Him through faith, worship, obedience, and service.

**Biblical references:** Ephesians 1:5–6, 12; Romans 11:36; Romans 15:13; Jude 24–25; 1 Corinthians 6:20; 1 Corinthians 10:31; Revelation 4:11; Psalm 16:11; Psalm 144:15; Revelation 21:3–4; Philippians 4:4.
